From 84d76908807376e7c6fa7e20d4be831a3ab0a494 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:20:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] temp/libcamera: faster and calmer autofocus

New libcamera patches:
0011 calculates the software ISP statistics for every second frame instead
of every fourth, so a focus step waits half as long,
0012 replaces the full sweep of the autofocus by a climb from the current
lens position: large steps where the sharpness curve is flat, coarse steps
near the peak, a turn when the first step clearly loses sharpness, and a
Gaussian fit through the best position and its neighbours instead of the
fine sweep. The lens is moved to its start position before the first
measurement, and a bad measurement next to the peak is taken once more.

Tuning for main, ultrawide and telephoto: flatStep/flatRatio for the
climb, a shorter warm-up and a change count of six statistics frames
(0.4 s), the telephoto camera with finer steps (128/384) for its shorter
lens range.

Measured on the same scene, time to focus after stream start: main
4.6 s -> 1.2 s, ultrawide 4.3 s -> 1.1 s, telephoto 2.7 s -> 0.6 s,
final positions within 1 % of the lens range of the old fine sweep.
