+From 5c276546a348b7759ef4bf1c10c09ff2c2f5a213 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:21:39 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 12/12] ipa: softisp: af: Climb from the current lens position
+
+Every scan ran the lens to the far end of its range and swept the whole
+range in coarse steps, followed by a fine sweep around the best position.
+That took up to 21 steps, and the lens visibly ran through the whole range
+even when the scene had changed only a little.
+
+Start the scan at the current lens position instead and climb the
+sharpness curve: large steps (flatStep) while the curve is flat, coarse
+steps once it rises, turn around when the first step clearly loses
+sharpness, and search the other side of the start position when the end
+of the range is reached without a peak. Replace the fine sweep by the top
+of a Gaussian fitted through the best position and its neighbours,
+measuring a missing neighbour at coarse step distance first. A scan
+without a clear peak ends in AfStateFailed.
+
+A neighbour of the peak that is less sharp than the sample beyond it is
+measured once more, as single bad measurements right after a lens move
+happen now and then.
+
+The lens keeps its position from the previous session, so move it to
+initialPosition (default: start of the range) before the first
+measurement.
+---
